course: dictionary
lesson: 7152
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 2
explain: The word perfect has several meanings, and the sentence around it tells you which one to use. «Teachers are pleased by a score of 100%; a perfect mark is not a sign of cheating.» Here perfect means with no mistakes at all. Swap in "a mistake-free mark" to check: it still makes sense, so you have the right meaning.
explain: Perfect can also mean exactly right for something, like the perfect present for a friend. It can mean complete too: a perfect stranger is someone you do not know at all. Read the words next to perfect and ask which meaning fits best.
explain: Perfect can also be a verb. To perfect something is to make it as good as it can be, often by practising. Perfects, perfected and perfecting all show this action. «Practice makes perfect» is a phrase you will hear often, and it means that practising helps you get better.
fact: Perfect (adjective) means with no mistakes or faults at all.
fact: Perfect means exactly right, as in a perfect fit or perfect timing.
fact: To perfect something is to make it as good as it can be, often by practising.
fact: In maths, a perfect square is made by multiplying a whole number by itself: 1, 4, 9, 16, 25.
fact: In grammar, the perfect tense uses have or has, like "I have finished". Nobody's perfect, and making mistakes is how we learn.
exercise: «Teachers are pleased by a score of 100%; a perfect mark is not a sign of cheating.» In this sentence, perfect means | Rushed and careless | Very loud and bright | Slightly old and worn | *With no mistakes at all
exercise: Mia says, «He is a perfect stranger.» What does perfect mean here? | Very famous and well known | *Complete: someone you do not know at all | A stranger who is never wrong | Very kind and friendly
exercise: Which of these is a perfect square? | 15 | 10 | *9 | 8
test: Which tense uses have or has, as in "I have finished"? | *The perfect tense | The past tense | The future tense | The present continuous tense
test: What does it mean to perfect a skill? | Sell it for money | Show it to a friend | *Make it as good as it can be, often by practising | Forget it completely
exam: «And if your clay owl cracks or you forget a line, you show it anyway and carry on, because the work and what you learned count, not only a perfect result.» In this sentence, perfect result means | A result that was done in a hurry | *A result with no faults at all | A result that is shared with everyone | A result that is very old
